# libsndfile -- the file I/O library pulseaudio's CLIENT takes as a bare
# dependency(), and the package this whole wave exists to reach.
#
# WHY A FILE-FORMAT LIBRARY IS ON THE PATH TO A SETTINGS DAEMON. pulseaudio's
# meson.build:615 is
#
#     sndfile_dep = dependency('sndfile', version : '>= 1.0.20')
#
# with no `required:` argument, which in meson means required: true -- and it
# sits in the block commented "Dependencies common to client, daemon and
# modules", ABOVE and outside `if get_option('daemon')`. So -Ddaemon=false does
# not reach it. There is no client-only pulseaudio without libsndfile, and no
# libpulse-mainloop-glib without a client-only pulseaudio, and no
# gnome-settings-daemon without libpulse-mainloop-glib.
#
# BLFS 12.4, pinned here rather than in versions.env: versions.env is
# regenerated wholesale from the LFS book by tools/pin-versions.sh, so a desktop
# pin placed there is destroyed by the next `make pin`.
SRC_URL=https://github.com/libsndfile/libsndfile/releases/download/1.2.2/libsndfile-1.2.2.tar.xz
SRC_SHA256=3799ca9924d3125038880367bf1468e53a1b7e3686a934f098b7e1d286cdb80e
SRC_DIR=libsndfile-1.2.2

# THE ALL-OR-NOTHING XIPH GROUP IS THE ONE THING TO UNDERSTAND ABOUT THIS
# RECIPE, and it is upstream's own description rather than an inference.
# configure.ac:321 tests the five probe results CONCATENATED:
#
#     AS_IF([test "x$ac_cv_flac$ac_cv_ogg$ac_cv_vorbis$ac_cv_vorbisenc$ac_cv_opus" \
#            = "xyesyesyesyesyes"], [ HAVE_EXTERNAL_XIPH_LIBS=1 ... ], [
#         AC_MSG_WARN([[*** One or more of the external libraries ... is missing]])
#         AC_MSG_WARN([[*** Unfortunately, for ease of maintenance, the external
#                         libs are an all or nothing affair.]])
#         enable_external_libs=no ])
#
# Five packages, one boolean, and the failure path is AC_MSG_WARN -- so ANY
# single one of libFLAC, libogg, libvorbis, libvorbisenc or libopus being
# absent, or present at too low a version, or present without its headers,
# removes support for ALL FIVE FORMATS from a build that stays green from
# configure through install. That is why this recipe declares all five rather
# than the two that are new in this wave, why install.sh asserts the outcome on
# the artefact, and why flac's own recipe asserts its libogg link: a soft
# failure three packages upstream lands HERE, and lands as silence.
#
# --disable-alsa. The option defaults to AUTODETECT and alsa-lib IS packaged
# here, so leaving it alone would resolve it -- finding 4's shape exactly. What
# it buys is an ALSA output backend for the `sndfile-play` demo program; what it
# costs is a real dependency edge on alsa-lib for a program nothing in this tree
# runs. Playback on this system goes through pipewire.
#
# --disable-sqlite. Same shape, same reason: sqlite is packaged (CRYPTO_PKGS),
# autodetection would find it, and its only consumer here is the regtest
# harness, which is not built and not installed.
#
# --disable-mpeg. LAME and mpg123 are not packaged, so this would fail soft
# today and switch itself on the day anybody packages either. Named so the
# artefact is a function of this file rather than of the builder image.
#
# --disable-static and --disable-full-suite are NOT both passed: only the first.
# --disable-full-suite would drop the sndfile-info/sndfile-convert programs and
# is tempting for a library-only package, but it also governs documentation and
# example installation in the same conditional (FULL_SUITE), and the programs
# cost nothing beyond the library this package already ships.
CONFIGURE_ARGS="--disable-static \
--disable-alsa \
--disable-sqlite \
--disable-mpeg"
